      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Competitive race but the ace draw should give CAPTAIN BELLASARIO (1) his chance. He has been tackling stronger opposition and was solid enough when fifth last week. Came from wider barriers for back-to-back seconds at this circuit and distance behind Len Smith Mile contenders Hi Manameisjeff and Dangerous last month. Those are good pointers for this. I GOT CHILLS NZ (2) drew widest and worked so was far from disgraced when beaten 6m last time. Up in grade but has won the last four times he has drawn three or lower so will relish this barrier. BETTERTHANCASH NZ (5) hasn't raced since August and is yet to win when fresh but a trial win suggests he is back in good order. This looks a suitable assignment so keep him safe. SAINT CRUSADER (9) may need luck from this barrier but he is going well with placings behind Swayzee and Hi Manameisjeff within his last three starts. Hard to knock the consistency of BUZZ BOMB (8) and he came from wider to win last week so respect.",
